 "_doc": "Registry of the published versions of the legal documents (plan 261022-documentos-legales). One entry per version: `id` is the document in user_legal_document_type, `web` its URL slug, `version` YYMMDD of its effective date in Europe/Madrid, `material` → requires_acceptance, `changes` the «what changes» per i18n file (none on a first version), `files` the frozen bytes per web language with their sha256 and, for the versions published before /documents, the old URL they keep serving (`legacy`). A frozen file never changes: the build refuses one whose bytes no longer match. `serial` grows with every change of what the manifest says (core refuses a lower one, or the same one with other bytes). A document may list `withdrawn` versions (out of `versions`); a version that comes before others already published lists in theirs `includes`. `reset` is the serial at which the history restarted (Israel, 04-11-2026, before launch: one version per document, the previous ones and their acceptances deleted): against a published manifest of a lower serial, signing it does not ask the old versions to stay.",
